      "inputTokens": 144,
      "outputTokens": 1069,
      "costUsd": 0.009692999999999998,
      "pronunciationText": "Now add up all the strips. This sign, a capital sigma, means add them all up. The sum of f of x times delta x, from a to b, estimates the total change from a to b. With four strips, using the heights at their left ends, the total is about one point one eight centimetres. The rate falls across every strip, and each rectangle uses the rate at its start, so each one reaches above the curve. That's an overestimate. The height can come from any x in the strip's base. Use the right ends, and every rectangle sits under the curve. That gives about zero point seven nine, an underestimate. The true amount is somewhere in between."
