      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 128,
      "outputTokens": 1006,
      "costUsd": 0.009118,
      "pronunciationText": "So make the strips thinner. Delta x is the whole interval, b minus a, split into n equal strips. So delta x equals b minus a, over n. Double n to eight, and the left sum drops to about one point one. Sixteen strips gives about one point zero five, and thirty-two gives about one point zero two. Meanwhile, the right sums climb towards the same place. Here's why. In a thinner strip, the rate changes less, so the gap between each rectangle and the curve shrinks. Both estimates close in on one centimetre. A later video shows why it's exactly one."
