      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 114,
      "outputTokens": 873,
      "costUsd": 0.007914,
      "pronunciationText": "Every estimate so far is an area. So the total change is the area of this region, between the curve and the x-axis, from a to b. That works when the curve stays on or above the axis, like this one. This curve is also continuous on the interval. Informally, that means you can draw it from one end to the other without taking the pen off the paper. If the rain stopped dead halfway, the graph would jump, and the pen would have to lift. In this topic, the curves we add up are continuous."
    },
