      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 113,
      "outputTokens": 894,
      "costUsd": 0.008102499999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Rectangles have flat tops, but the curve slopes. So join the top points with straight lines instead. Each strip becomes a trapezium, a shape with two parallel sides. Its area is the average of the two heights, times the width. That's the average of the left rectangle and the right rectangle. With just four trapezia, the estimate is about zero point nine eight seven. That's closer than thirty-two rectangles. Here the curve bends downwards, so each straight top sits just under it, and the trapezia slightly underestimate."
