      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 159,
      "outputTokens": 1140,
      "costUsd": 0.0103395,
      "pronunciationText": "Let's compare the methods on one example. A trolley's speed is x squared metres per second, x seconds after it starts. Estimate how far it goes in the first two seconds, using four strips. Speed times time is distance, so each strip's area is a distance. Delta x is two minus zero, over four, which is a half. The heights at zero, a half, one, one and a half and two are zero, a quarter, one, two and a quarter, and four. Left rectangles use the first four heights, which gives a half times three and a half, or one point seven five metres. Right rectangles use the last four, which gives three point seven five. The trapezia take the average, two point seven five."
    },
