      "pronunciationText": "Now refine all three in a graphing app. At eight strips, the left rectangles give about two point one nine, the right about three point one nine, and the trapezia about two point six nine. At sixteen strips, the trapezia give about two point six seven two. All three settle near two point six six seven metres. Now look at the errors. Each time n doubles, the rectangle errors roughly halve. But the trapezium error drops to about a quarter. This curve bends upwards, so the trapezia sit just above it, and slightly overestimate. Here the trapezia improve fastest. Try it yourself in a graphing app: change n and compare."
